{"id": "be26cb00-b7de-4857-a128-09e7f4bc57dd", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check how Bedrock is being invoked in this account in us-east-1 over the last 14 days. I'll look for model invocation logging, CloudTrail records, and CloudWatch metrics to see which calls use a bare model ID and which use an inference profile.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_fe2BuyrlNumqBI2OOJmkyk", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "bedrock-model-id-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["searching-logs", "investigating-infrastructure-changes", "exploring-metrics"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Determine whether any Amazon Bedrock runtime calls (InvokeModel, InvokeModelWithResponseStream, Converse, ConverseStream) in us-east-1 use a bare foundation-model ID (e.g. anthropic.claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022-v2:0 or a foundation-model ARN) where an inference profile (system-defined like us.anthropic.* / global.* or application inference profile ARN) should be used instead. Identify which callers (IAM principal / role / user agent / source) are doing this, how many calls, and which model IDs.",
  "context": "User asked: 'Are any of our Bedrock calls in us-east-1 using a bare model ID where they should use an inference profile?' Read-only audit, answer will be relayed in chat. Account 012345678901_1, region us-east-1. Approach hints: (1) check bedrock get_model_invocation_logging_configuration to see if invocation logging to CloudWatch Logs/S3 is enabled; if so query it for the modelId field in the window and classify each as bare model ID vs inference profile (ID prefixed with a geo like us./eu./apac./global. or ARN containing ':inference-profile/' or ':application-inference-profile/'). (2) Check CloudTrail (via lookup_cloudtrail_events and/or CloudTrail Lake / trail S3 or CloudWatch log group if data events for Bedrock are captured) for Bedrock events; note Bedrock InvokeModel is a data event and may not be recorded unless configured. (3) Check CloudWatch AWS/Bedrock metrics (ModelId dimension) for invocations per model ID in the window, and note which model IDs are in use. (4) Also list inference profiles available (list_inference_profiles) and check for any models that are only invocable through inference profiles in us-east-1 (those would fail with bare IDs - look for ValidationException 'on-demand throughput isn't supported' errors in logs/metrics InvocationClientErrors). (5) If useful, check Lambda/ECS/EKS config environment variables or code for hardcoded MODEL_ID values as supporting evidence, but keep it bounded. Be explicit about what data source you could and could not access and about any coverage gaps; do not claim 'none found' if there was no data source that would have shown it.",
  "resources": ["AWS account 012345678901_1", "us-east-1", "Bedrock runtime", "CloudWatch namespace AWS/Bedrock"],
  "timeframe": "2026-11-10T18:57:18Z/2026-11-24T18:57:18Z",
  "criteria": "Return: data sources available, per-model-ID call counts classified as bare vs inference profile, callers using bare IDs, any related errors, and clear statement of coverage limitations. Read-only; make no changes."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit Bedrock model ID usage in us-east-1 over 14 days"}], "created_at": null}

